# edgedetectdepth

- Label: Edge Detect by Depth
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 5 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/edgedetectdepth.html
- Summary (EN): Finds silhouette lines where one surface blocks another and varies their width, by comparing depth values with neighbours using ray differentials.
- Résumé (FR) : Trace les lignes de silhouette où une surface en masque une autre, à partir d'une carte de profondeur.

- Inputs meaning: ["depth: Z-depth values used to find self-occluding lines", "thickness: optional input varying line width"]

- Key parameters: ["Thickness Scale: kernel radius in pixels; a multiplier when thickness is connected", "Edge Spread: multiplies the Gaussian weight spread", "Blur: blurs the input before detection", "Depth Tolerance: minimum Z-depth difference from neighbours for a pixel to count as part of the line", "Min Probe Radius: smallest search radius for probe pixels"]

- Caveats: ["Detects only self-occluding silhouettes, not contour or crease lines.", "The page gives no default values or value ranges."]

